.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the macOS installer and lifecycle CLI for
.Lk https://github.com/Crosstalk-Solutions/project-nomad "Project NOMAD" ,
an offline AI + knowledge server.
The CLI sits above the admin-layer patches contributed by the macOS community
fork lineage (snfettig, NoamanKhalil, proximasan), providing a single-file
bash entry point for installation, lifecycle management, model pulls,
benchmarking, and recovery operations.
.Pp
On Apple Silicon, the installer runs Ollama natively (Metal-accelerated) while
the admin/MySQL/Redis stack runs in OrbStack containers. Storage is split
between always-internal hot state (mysql, redis under
.Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/state )
and a configurable cold content root
.Pa ${NOMAD_DATA_ROOT}
that may be on an external drive and safely unplugged.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "upgrade-models"
.It Cm install
Run the full install pipeline: dependency bootstrap (Xcode CLT, Homebrew, jq,
Rosetta 2), data root selection, OrbStack install + memory tune, native Ollama
+ LaunchAgent, secrets generation, container stack pull and bring-up, admin
health-check, native-Ollama wiring via the admin API, model pulls, and
benchmark host-info auto-patcher LaunchAgent. Idempotent — safe to re-run.
.Pp
Options:
.Bl -tag -width "--no-models"
.It Fl -data-root Ar PATH
Path for cold content (Wikipedia ZIMs, Ollama models, Kolibri, ProtoMaps).
Default: prompt for internal vs external drive choice.
.It Fl -tier Ar TIER
Model preset to pull. One of:
.Cm auto , tiny , small , medium , large , xl , dreamy .
Default:
.Cm auto
(picks based on
.Ev hw.memsize ).
.It Fl -models Ar "names..."
Explicit space-separated model list, overrides
.Fl -tier .
.It Fl -no-models
Skip model pulls entirely.
.It Fl -yes , Fl y
Auto-confirm prompts (for unattended runs).
.El
.It Cm check Op Ar section
Read-only diagnostic. Sections: system (RAM, ports, network, Rosetta),
stack (containers, native Ollama, admin API, download queue, Wikipedia state),
install (pre-flight inventory with skip/install/fix plan).
Default:
.Cm all .
Output also written to a timestamped log file in the bundle folder for
iCloud-sync inspection.
.It Cm up | down
Bring the compose stack up or down. Native Ollama LaunchAgent is unaffected
by either command.
.It Cm restart Op Ar SERVICE
Restart a compose service. Default: admin.
.It Cm logs Op Ar SERVICE
Snapshot the last 100 lines of a service's logs. Default: admin. Pass
.Fl f
for follow mode (e.g.
.Nm Cm logs Fl f Cm admin Ns ).
.It Cm models Op Cm list | pull Ar TIER|NAMES...
List installed models with fits-this-Mac verdict, or pull a tier or specific
named models via native Ollama API. With no subargs, lists.
.It Cm benchmark Op Cm run | patch-host Op Ar MODEL
Run native-Metal vs container-Rosetta tokens/sec comparison on the same
model, or patch admin's latest benchmark row with this Mac's real CPU/GPU
hardware. Default model:
.Cm llama3.1:8b .
.It Cm downloads Op Cm list | cancel | remove Op Ar JOBID
List or manage admin's BullMQ download queue (Wikipedia ZIMs, model pulls,
ProtoMaps regions). Uses the admin REST API.
.It Cm zim Op Cm list | wikipedia | remote
Manage installed ZIM files. With
.Cm wikipedia ,
manages the Wikipedia variant selection (state or select).
.It Cm services Op Cm list | install | affect
Inspect or manage admin-spawned content services (Kiwix, Qdrant, Kolibri,
FlatNotes). Uses the admin REST API.
.It Cm system Op Cm info | debug | internet
Inspect admin's view of the system (CPU, memory, services, internet
reachability) via its REST API.
.It Cm api Ar PATH Op Ar JSON_BODY
Raw admin API call. Generic escape hatch for endpoints not wrapped by other
subcommands. PATH is e.g.
.Pa /api/system/services
or
.Pa /api/ollama/configure-remote .
.It Cm orbstack-tune Op Ar GB
Tune OrbStack VM memory. With no arg, computes 80% of host RAM (proportional
formula, scales 8 GB Air → 192+ GB Studio). With explicit GB, sets that
allocation. Restarts OrbStack VM to apply (~10s downtime). Run during
install automatically; this is the manual entry point for re-tuning.
.It Cm reset-ollama
Recover from stuck LaunchAgent state ("bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output
error"). Bootouts existing agent, kills orphan ollama serves, re-bootstraps.
.It Cm fix-kiwix
Manual trigger of the kiwix self-heal pass. Background: admin's downloader
writes ZIM files directly to
.Pa /data/ Ns Ar name Ns .zim
with no
.Pa .tmp
suffix during download. kiwix-serve is launched with the shell glob
.Cm *.zim
which expands to ALL files in
.Pa /data
including in-progress ones. Partial files have valid filenames and invalid
libzim headers, so kiwix-serve crashes on the first one it encounters and
the
.Cm unless-stopped
restart policy puts it in a crash loop.
.Pp
Self-heal reads kiwix's own log for the line
.Dq Unable to add the ZIM file 'X' to the internal library.\& ,
moves
.Pa X
to
.Pa storage/zim-inprogress/ ,
restarts kiwix, repeats up to 5 passes per run. The
.Cm com.projectnomad.kiwix-self-heal
LaunchAgent runs the same logic every 60 seconds automatically — this
subcommand triggers an immediate run plus verbose output (current state,
recent action-log entries, final state, quarantine listing). Useful for:
fixing kiwix without waiting for the next 60s tick; understanding what
prior auto-runs did. The action log is at
.Pa ~/Library/Logs/nomad-kiwix-self-heal.action.log .
Upstream fix worth filing: admin's downloader should write
.Pa name.zim.downloading
and rename atomically on completion.
.It Cm stl Op Cm list | scan | import | path Op Ar DIR Op Ar CATEGORY
Workshop / Offline STL Library — host-side ops for the 3D-printable file
catalog at
.Pa ${NOMAD_DATA_ROOT}/storage/stl-library/ .
.Pp
.Cm list
calls
.Pa /api/workshop?per_page=200
and pretty-prints the admin's catalog.
.Cm scan
triggers a server-side rescan (same code path as the UI's Rescan button) —
walks the library tree, upserts the
.Cm stl_files
index, removes orphan rows for deleted files, generates missing
thumbnails via
.Xr stl-thumb 1 .
.Cm import Ar DIR Op Ar CATEGORY
copies every
.Pa *.stl
and
.Pa *.3mf
under
.Ar DIR
into
.Pa storage/stl-library/<CATEGORY>/
(default
.Cm other )
and triggers a rescan. Existing files in the library are not overwritten;
re-running
.Cm import
just skips them.
.Cm path
prints the absolute library root on the host (useful for shell scripting).
Categories:
.Cm medical , tools , household , replacement-parts , agriculture ,
.Cm firearm-accessories , other .
.It Cm reinstall
Nuclear path: full
.Cm uninstall
(including data drive contents with confirm) followed by
.Cm install .
One confirmation prompt up front, fully unattended after.
.It Cm uninstall
Remove all NOMAD containers + named volumes + networks, the Ollama
LaunchAgent + plist, the benchmark patcher LaunchAgent, secrets at
.Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/.env ,
and (with confirm) data drive contents. Preserves Homebrew, OrbStack, and
Ollama themselves (other apps may depend on them).
.It Cm upgrade-models
Re-pull all currently-installed Ollama models at their latest tag.
.It Cm help
Print short usage. Full reference is this manpage.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "NOMAD_STATE_ROOT"
.It Ev NOMAD_DATA_ROOT
Cold content root (Wikipedia ZIMs, models, maps). Set in
.Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/.env
at install. Typically an external APFS drive but may be internal.
.It Ev NOMAD_STATE_ROOT
Hot state root (mysql, redis). Always
.Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/state
on internal disk. Survives data-drive eject.
.It Ev APPLE_CHIP_MODEL , Ev APPLE_GPU_MODEL
Host hardware identifiers passed to admin so it can identify the real Apple
Silicon chip via
.Pa si.cpu()
fallback. Captured at install via
.Pa system_profiler .
.It Ev NOMAD_ADMIN_IMAGE , Ev NOMAD_UPDATER_IMAGE
GHCR image overrides. Default to proximasan's multi-arch images. Falls back
to upstream amd64 (Rosetta-emulated) if the proximasan pull fails.
.It Ev NOMAD_YES
Set to
.Cm 1
to auto-confirm prompts. Equivalent to
.Fl -yes .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.config/project-nomad/state/"
.It Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/.env
Generated secrets (chmod 600). APP_KEY, MySQL passwords, NOMAD_DATA_ROOT,
NOMAD_STATE_ROOT, APPLE_CHIP_MODEL, APPLE_GPU_MODEL.
.It Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/state/
Always-internal mysql + redis bind mounts.
.It Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/ollama-launcher.sh
Wrapper script run by the Ollama LaunchAgent. Resolves the data drive at
runtime so renamed mounts don't break the daemon.
.It Pa ~/.config/project-nomad/benchmark-patcher.sh
Background script run every 30 seconds by the benchmark-patcher LaunchAgent.
Fills in real Apple chip + Metal GPU on
.Pa benchmark_results
rows.
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.projectnomad.ollama.plist
Native Ollama LaunchAgent (port 11434, KV-cache q8_0, 4 parallel,
RAM-scaled max-loaded-models).
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.projectnomad.benchmark-patcher.plist
Auto-patcher LaunchAgent.
.It Pa ${NOMAD_DATA_ROOT}/storage/
Admin's storage mount: ZIMs, Kolibri, Qdrant vectors, FlatNotes, ProtoMaps.
.It Pa ${NOMAD_DATA_ROOT}/ollama-models/
Native Ollama model weights.
.It Pa ${NOMAD_DATA_ROOT}/quick-chat.html
Portable browser chat UI dropped onto the data drive. Plug the drive into
any Mac, open this file — page bootstraps Ollama if missing and connects.
.It Pa ${NOMAD_DATA_ROOT}/quick-chat.sh
Companion script for the HTML page; auto-installs Ollama via Homebrew if
needed, sets OLLAMA_MODELS, starts the daemon, opens the HTML.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# First install on a fresh Mac
bash nomad install

# Pre-flight inventory (read-only, what would 'install' touch?)
nomad check install

# Pull a different model tier on existing install
nomad models pull large

# Diagnose why the leaderboard shows wrong CPU
nomad benchmark patch-host

# Bring stack down before unplugging the data drive
nomad down

# After replug
nomad up

# One-command nuke and fresh install
nomad reinstall

# Hit any admin endpoint directly
nomad api /api/system/services
nomad api /api/zim/wikipedia/select '{"optionId":"all-mini"}'
.Ed
